<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12450" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dĕcennis</span></b> , e, adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of ten years</i> (post-Aug.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bellum, of the Greeks before Troy,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 8, 4, 22</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">also proelium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 89, 2, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">obsidio (Veiorum),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Flor.
					1, 12, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">equae,</span>”
				<i>ten years old</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin. 8, 44, 69</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">decenni major asinus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pall. Mart. 14, 1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">decennia</span></b> , ium, n., = decennalia,
				<i>a festival under the emperors, held every ten
				years</i>, Treb. Gall. 5 <i>fin.</i>; cf.:
			decennalis, <i>no.</i> II.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
